WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.630
In the battle with Archbishop Orwell,

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:07.290
in which she tried to use Akari's Pure Concept of Time
to regain her youth,

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:11.290
I came in contact with Akari's consciousness
and realized something.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:17.920
Akari had rewound time back several months
to relive the time she had spent with me.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.960
The reason she was so friendly from the moment we
met was a remnant of what she had already experienced.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:28.580
That means despite earning so much of Akari's trust,
I somehow failed to kill her.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:33.250
That's why this time, I'll make sure I kill Akari.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.750
Deep within me,
there's another personality I don't even know about.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:44.380
It's the true Akari Tokitou,
who remembers everything from before I regressed.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.880
The true me rewound time just so
I could prevent Menou's death.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.880
Don't you die, Menou.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.170
And this time...

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.630
Make sure you kill me properly.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.380
"These gates are open to any who wish to pass through."

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:09.040
"Be they healthy, ill, happy, unhappy,

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.880
diligent, slothful, wise, foolish..."

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.330
"be they devout followers or any kind of heretic,"

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.170
"be they pure or evil of heart,"

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.670
"these holy gates are open unto them."

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.000
It's a quote that represents the spirit of pilgrimage.
I like these words.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:31.460
They say leaving through these gates and finishing
the journey absolves people of all of their sins,

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.880
and that they're reborn anew.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.460
I see they issued you a new scripture, Menou.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:40.960
Yes. The acting archbishop arranged it for me.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.170
I also got enough travel funds for the time being,
so we can set off without any worries.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.580
Yeah, off we go on a pilgrimage!

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.540
...Yes.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.580
Our destination is the Sanctuary.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.880
It's on this pilgrimage route, way off at the very end.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.040
Right.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:01.880
There's a residential area for Lost Ones
there that can take me in, right?

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.920
But even if the trip is smooth it
will still take about three months.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.790
No problem! As long as I'm with you.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:10.500
Then let's get going.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.000
Oh hey. Wait, Menou.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.960
As long as we're doing this,
let's take the first step together.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:16.920
Please?

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.000
Oh, all right. Sure.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:20.960
Okay, here we go.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:23.040
Ready, and...

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.540
That's right, this is a fresh new step,

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:34.460
toward finding a way to kill Akari and carrying
out the deed with my very own hands.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.790
<b>Episode 7: Port City of Libelle</b>

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.000
Hey, Menou.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:34.580
This place... Uh, the "wilderness area," was it?

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.170
You mean the Wild Frontier?

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:41.460
The environment is so harsh that humans
gave up on pioneering it altogether.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:45.880
Stretches of it lie in between the countries.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.500
Didn't you say there are scary creatures out here?

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.830
The monsters. Yes, there are.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:55.000
There are also outlaws around who
call themselves "adventurers."

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.000
The area seems awfully normal, considering.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.880
This is the pilgrimage route, so it's relatively safe.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.540
But we'll see just how long you're so optimistic.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:09.540
I'll be just fine! This is gonna be a breeze!

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:15.040
Come on, Menou! Hurry, hurry!

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.000
Fine, fine.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.460
<b>Two weeks later</b>

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.710
I can't go on anymore!

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.830
Like I said, it's only a bit farther.

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:25.960
This is wearing down my soul!

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:29.210
If it was, you wouldn't be saying that.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.500
Well, that's true.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:35.000
When you're really worn down,
you don't even have the energy to complain.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.130
Then okay!

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:42.580
Want to know why my soul is still fulfilled,
even on such a tough journey?

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:43.380
Not really.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.500
You really do, huh?!

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.420
It's because...

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:51.040
You, my emotional oasis-is right by my side.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:59.210
Meanwhile, I think you're draining me of all of my energy.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:02.210
Can't you find a more self-sufficient
way to boost your spirits?

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:06.040
I can only get Menou nutrients from the real thing.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.500
I'll shrivel up if I don't get enough!

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.960
No you won't.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:12.920
You lived just fine for sixteen years before you met me!

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:16.040
I have no recollection of those sixteen years anymore.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:20.540
It's all about today, Menou.
We're young and we should only live in the present.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:24.500
You should look back on the past and
think about the future at least a little bit.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.000
Look, our future is coming into view.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:33.420
Wow, it's a town! The ocean's so big! And blue!

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:37.750
It's the Port City of Libelle. It's nice and relaxing.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.790
Ooh, I can't wait!

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:42.830
Look, it's the ocean.

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:45.380
Right.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.420
It's the first time you see it, isn't it?

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:48.380
Yes.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:51.130
Don't you have anything to say?

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:52.500
It's big.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.710
Is that all?

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.170
It's blue.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:00.630
You really are so emotionless, girl.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:04.670
Master.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:06.790
Is that fog?

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:11.170
"Fog," hmm? Technically, not quite.

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:14.710
That's none other than one of the
Four Major Human Errors scattered around the world:

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:17.000
The Pandemonium.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:23.540
Sealed away in there is a calamity
that almost destroyed the world.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:26.790
Those who enter can never hope to come out again.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.630
A prison of fog.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.670
Hey.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.630
Do you think those are clouds?

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:36.420
If the weather's going to take a turn,
we should hurry, right?

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:38.540
Don't worry about that.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:39.710
Really?

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:40.420
Yes...

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.880
That thing is always there.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.750
I need to stop by somewhere, so I'm going on ahead.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.630
Wait for me, Menou!

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.000
We will be sure to process your request.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:58.330
I'll be back. Thank you.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.630
Menou! Are you done?

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:05.380
Yes.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:10.540
But I can't believe you have to apply for travel
funds at a church in every town we come across.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:14.460
They're providing us with money. I can't complain.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:17.460
And I guess we get to see the sights as a bonus.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.130
Hey, Menou!

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.130
There's somewhere I want to check out!

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:26.130
There! The island with the castle!

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.250
Oh, you mean Libelle Island.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:31.040
Unfortunately, we can't go there.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:32.540
Why not?

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:37.420
That island is the private property of Count Libelle,
a dignitary of the city.

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:41.130
We can't go unless we're on special business
or there's an event or something.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.710
Aw, I see.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:47.420
Don't be so discouraged.
There are plenty of other places to see here.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.750
Are you sure?

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:52.460
It was a long two weeks on the road.
Why don't we splurge a bit?

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:54.130
"Splurge"?!

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:56.040
Yeah, yeah! Let's do it!

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.080
Let's go then! Come on!

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:58.830
Fine, fine.

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:02.330
Flare's successor, Flarette, hmm?

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.330
Yes...

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:06.000
I remember her...

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.250
<b>Public bath</b>

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:12.750
This is so nice...

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:16.750
I'm glad you seem to be enjoying this.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.670
Well, the fact that your idea of "splurging"

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:23.790
is the public bath goes to show how strapped
for money you've been, but anyway.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.960
That's not it. It shows I live in honorable poverty.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.710
I know, I know.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:33.290
You're pure, just, and strong, as a priestess should be.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.040
Hey, Menou.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:39.040
Our destination on this journey is some
place called "the Sanctuary," right?

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:40.500
That's right.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:44.290
If I go there, they'll take me in.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:47.250
But you know, I've been kind of thinking...

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:51.500
It wouldn't be so bad if I kept
traveling around this world...

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:54.500
With you, Menou.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.130
Don't be silly.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:00.670
The point of a journey is to get to a destination.

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:04.710
I don't know. I like taking side trips, too.

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:05.630
Whatever.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.790
I'm getting out before you.

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:17.670
Go ahead.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.540
Akari will be in there a little while longer.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.040
Okay!

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:23.000
Menou!

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:25.920
Oooh, I haven't seen you in two weeks!

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:31.500
I can feel your warmth. You're mine. All mine!

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.380
I don't share you with anyone else, Menou!

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:36.040
Okay, okay. I'm impressed though, Momo.

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:41.420
You traveled the Wild Frontier away from the pilgrimage
route and still managed to get here before us.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:42.880
It was nothing!

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:49.130
Well, I did get harassed a bit by that
crappy little princess again on the way.

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:50.670
Princess Ashuna?

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:54.710
Why would the princess of Grisarika
come all the way out here?

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:55.630
Who knows?

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.290
She probably has a thirst for battle or something.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:00.880
"A thirst for battle"?

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:10.080
Anyway, I beat her down into the danger zone
of some ancient ruins and left her there.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.920
If I'm lucky, she's already dead.

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:19.580
I see...

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:24.040
Anyway, how long do you intend to stay here in Libelle?

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.920
What? Why?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:31.210
Don't you remember this town is famous
for teeming with those people?

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.790
"Those people"...

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.750
Oh, do you mean the Fourth?

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.130
Yes. Despicable, aren't they?

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:42.250
They insist they're a liberated Fourth class
who aren't Faust or Noblesse or Commons,

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:44.750
yet all they do is engage in random acts of terror.

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:46.500
They don't make any sense.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.040
But they had quite a movement going for a while.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:54.710
If our Master hadn't captured
their leader a few years ago,

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:59.330
they may have been a threat to the world even now.

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:00.790
Yes, exactly.

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:05.880
I figure the Fourth have a grudge against Master Flare.

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:07.500
Well yes, perhaps.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:12.580
And you're called Flarette, "Flare's successor," you know?

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.250
So I need to be careful.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:18.210
Yes. Not that I'm too worried about you.

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:24.380
I did look into the Fourth in town just in case,
so I'll send the details to your scripture later.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:28.330
Thanks, Momo. I'm proud to have such a capable aide.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:31.420
Well, you have every right to be proud.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:35.080
More praise, pleeaase!

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:36.130
There, there.

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:41.580
Sounds like Akari's about to come out.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:42.830
Awww.

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:44.670
Oh, by the way!

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:49.830
Speaking of Boobalicious,
are you not going to try out the Pandemonium?

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:55.130
Otherworlder or not,
she might not be able to escape if you toss her in there.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:13:00.330
There might even be some crazy
monster inside that would eat her for us.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.540
Th-that's true.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:06.040
Don't tell me you hadn't even considered it?

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:08.880
I hadn't. I completely spaced out.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:14.130
It's definitely more promising than the usual methods.
It may be worth a try.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:15.920
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:18.710
That was an awfully long bath, Akari.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:20.710
This is normal for a Japanese person.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:21.750
It is?

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:25.670
Hey, Menou. Weren't you just talking to someone?

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.460
No, I wasn't.

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:29.750
Come on, Akari. Sit down there.

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:31.500
I'll dry your hair for you.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:32.670
Okay!

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.750
This is just what I was worried about.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:38.380
Menou isn't sure about killing that girl...

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.460
Am I hesitating?

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:42.880
No, that can't be right.

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:46.290
Thank you, Menou.

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:48.210
I'm an Executioner.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:50.960
And the job of an Executioner...

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.290
is to kill Lost Ones.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:06.170
Libelle is such an interesting place!

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:10.960
The area has lots of hills,
so the buildings were designed to accommodate that.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:12.330
Yeah!

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:16.790
The title would be, "The Ocean, the Town, and Menou."

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.210
Yeah, what a great shot!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:22.580
Thanks, I guess. I'm glad you're having fun.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:25.290
Yeah, I'm glad I'm having fun, too!

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:29.380
But it's really too bad we can't go over there.

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:31.250
It's such a lovely castle.

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:35.330
Like I said yesterday, we can't set foot on that island.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:39.880
But, we can look at it up close from the sea.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:44.000
I'm sure we could borrow the church's boat.
Want to go?

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:44.790
Really?!

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:48.130
You can steer a boat, Menou?

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:52.750
I'm a pure, just, and strong priestess,
pretty much capable of anything.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.210
Just leave it up to me!

00:14:57.380 --> 00:15:01.250
Wahoo! This feels great!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.960
That's dangerous. Will you sit down?

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.830
And did you take that nausea medication I gave you?

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:08.540
Oh, that's right.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.670
We're getting closer to the castle!

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:23.000
Did you say it belongs to a count?

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:23.830
Yes.

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:27.380
But, ever since Count Libelle fell ill,

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:30.710
his only daughter has been acting on his behalf.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:32.670
Apparently she's still in her teens.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:36.000
Wow... Menou, you really know a lot, huh?

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.920
I just heard about it at the church yesterday.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.710
Though it was really from Momo.
That must be tough,<b></b>

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:42.630
being acting head of a household around my age.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:47.880
One of the initial members of the Fourth,
Count Libelle also funded their operations.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.630
Now in his place,

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:55.500
the person put in place as the leader of the Fourth in
this city is his daughter, Manon Libelle.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:00.250
Are we sure she's in town now?

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:06.420
She was spotted on the pilgrimage route.
Considering the timing, she must be.

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:12.130
Why does it have to be the successor of Flare,
the sworn enemy of the Fourth?

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.630
Is she strong, this woman?

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:18.630
Rumor has it that she's the one who
took down Archbishop Orwell.

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:20.710
We can't underestimate her.

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:22.290
Lady Manon.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:23.170
Yes?

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:27.880
Please share your thoughts on behalf of Count Libelle.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:31.540
Um, why don't we just watch her for a while?

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.630
Perhaps she'll simply move on without doing anything.

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:38.500
Honestly, Lady Manon.

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:43.170
Well, perhaps you're too young to know
how much of a threat Flare was-

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:44.380
I do.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:49.250
My mother was killed by none other than her, after all.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:56.880
She was a useless woman,
considering the trouble we went through to get her.

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:02.500
In any case, we must do something about Flarette.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:06.290
Before it affects the distribution of our product.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.960
I'll go and make a preemptive attack.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.880
I assume that's all right with you, Lady Manon?

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:14.380
Yes. I'll be sure to tell my father.

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:15.080
Well, then...

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:22.790
I must take my leave now,
but I hope you will all enjoy the sandwiches.

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:26.130
It would be a shame to throw them out.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:33.380
She's only a child, after all. We can't count on her.

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:38.380
Well, at least the food she serves tastes good. I'll give her that.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:49.000
The Pandemonium...

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:55.130
A prison of fog that they say is easy enough to enter,
but impossible to escape from.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:00.210
Even for Akari,
who can revive herself by regressing time...

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:01.540
This might just work.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:04.210
I see the drug has taken its effect.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:27.580
<b><i>Auto Etheric Connect (Condition: Met) - Improper Attachment</i></b>

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:27.580
<b><i>Pure Concept [Time] - Unlock</i></b>

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:34.920
Where am I?

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:37.920
Oh, right. It's Libelle.

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:43.210
I'm in the Pandemonium, so everything must be on track.

00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:45.830
Yup, glad everything's going smoothly.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:48.630
Whoa, there!

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:54.290
I have to get swallowed by that thing again?

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:56.000
How many times has it been?

00:18:56.290 --> 00:18:58.420
It feels awful in there.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:01.130
But, this place can't kill me.

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:04.380
Sorry, Menou.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.080
What's this light?

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.540
This wasn't here the last time...

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:20.380
If Akari dies here, this journey will be over.

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:26.960
After that, nothing changes.
I'll just go back to life as an Executioner.

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:31.040
But, what's this pain I feel in my heart?

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:32.460
Is it guilt?

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:37.170
No, I don't deserve to suffer from that kind of thing.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.540
Ooh, ouch!

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:51.710
Uh, what? Why did I just bump my head?

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:54.500
Wasn't I looking up at the castle?

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.790
That's weird.

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:58.210
What are you saying?

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:01.290
After you finished seeing the
castle you said you were sleepy,

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:02.880
and snoozed off like an idiot, remember?

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:06.040
And now you're suddenly up and all confused.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:07.330
What, really?

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:11.580
Sorry Menou, after the trouble of bringing me here.

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:13.130
It's fine.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:17.460
Hey, were you actually sad being left alone for a while?

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:19.460
As if!

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:22.460
I was grateful to get a bit of peace and quiet.

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:23.750
Hey, that's mean!

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:27.290
It would be nice to say you were sad,
even if you weren't.

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:28.670
Fine, whatever.

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:30.920
We're going back.

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:33.330
My hair will get damaged from the ocean breeze.

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:36.750
Hey, Menou?

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.000
What?

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.210
You know why I slept so well?

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:46.170
I think it's because I feel so safe next to you, Menou.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:49.460
That's true.

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:54.960
The fact that Akari currently revives next
to me is probably because of that.

00:20:55.790 --> 00:20:59.630
But by using her Pure Concept,

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:03.000
Akari is another step closer to
letting her power get out of control.

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:05.790
I'm sure we're still okay...

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:07.540
What do you mean, "okay"?

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:12.710
I mean this.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.080
Wait, what?!

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.290
It's been bothering me a bit since I saw you in the bath.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.710
I think you're still okay, just barely.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:22.170
Hey! What do you mean, "just barely"?!

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:26.830
Someone's in a good mood.

00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:29.540
Come, this way.

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.130
Go ahead.

00:21:48.790 --> 00:21:51.920
Whew, I'm quite hungry.

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:54.040
Let's see, what should I eat?

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:58.920
Oh, I know. Perhaps I should go to the market.

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>Monstrine</b>

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:39.250
Next episode: Monstrine.
